3. Permissions  hub

Who you are to the system, and what decides whether you may read, write or run
something.

On your machine
  User      alice (uid 1000, gid 1000)
  Groups    alice, wheel, docker, 4242
  Admin     member of wheel: the group sudo usually trusts
  Umask     0022: new files 644 (rw-r--r--), new folders 755

  Modules   capability, landlock, yama, apparmor
  AppArmor  enabled · profiles: 2 enforce, 1 complain

Commands
  id                      your user, your groups
  ls -l file              owner, group and rights of a file
  namei -l /path/to/file  rights of every folder on the way to a file
  sudo -l                 what sudo lets you run
  getfacl file            extra users and groups allowed (ACL)
  getenforce              SELinux mode, on Fedora and RHEL

Paths
  /etc/passwd      accounts: uid, home folder, shell
  /etc/group       groups and their members
  /etc/sudoers.d/  who may use sudo, and for what

Cards
  idk 3.1  rwx, octal and umask
  idk 3.2  setuid, setgid and sticky bit
  idk 3.3  sudo and groups
  idk 3.4  ACLs and capabilities
  idk 3.5  SELinux and AppArmor
